          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On October 8, 1954, at 11:30 PM, four witnesses observed a circular, luminous object in the sky. The phenomenon moved from east to west. The observation lasted for a few seconds. This observation was the subject of a concise intelligence report by the National Gendarmerie. This type of observation can have various origins (sunlight reflection on an airplane, balloon, meteor, etc.). The GEIPAN classified this case as C due to the lack of information.",
